We denote the length of these successive vacations to be 
\begin_inset Formula $V_{1}$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $V_{2}$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\dots$
\end_inset 

.
 We assume that 
\begin_inset Formula $V_{1},$
\end_inset 


\begin_inset Formula $V_{2}$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\dots$
\end_inset 

 are i.i.d.
 random variables which are also independent of the customer times and the
 service times.
 We can then attempt to compute the mean residual service time for this
 queue for a 
\emph on 
Poisson (Markov) arrival
\emph default 
 system with 
\emph on 
general service times
\emph default 
 and 
\emph on 
generally distributed vacation times
\emph default 
.
